  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "The points \\((6,12)\\) and \\((0,-6)\\) are connected by a straight line. Another point on this line is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\((3,3)\\)",
    "B": "\\((2,1)\\)",
    "C": "\\((7,16)\\)",
    "D": "\\((-1,-4)\\)",
    "E": "\\((-3,-8)\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The midpoint of the segment joining the given points must lie on their line. Moving halfway along a segment halves both coordinate changes, so the midpoint coordinates are the averages of the endpoint coordinates:\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{6+0}{2},\\frac{12+(-6)}{2}\\right)=(3,3).\n\\]\nThus another point on the line is \\((3,3)\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
